From: MYIR Tech <support@myirtech.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] frontend: keep DRM compositor alive without connected outputs

The DRM backend creates heads for disconnected connectors and keeps its udev
hotplug monitor active. This allows a connector that becomes connected later
to create and enable an output without restarting Weston.

However, REQUIRE_OUTPUTS_ANY currently treats an empty layoutput list as an
error because both failed_layoutputs and the list length are zero. This makes
Weston exit during initialisation when no monitor is connected, before the DRM
backend can receive a later hotplug event.

Do not fail the initialisation when no layoutput was attempted. Preserve the
existing failure policy when one or more detected outputs actually fail to
enable.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [i.MX8MP product startup policy]
Signed-off-by: MYIR Tech <support@myirtech.com>
---
 frontend/main.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/frontend/main.c b/frontend/main.c
index bea7ad51..35cabd4a 100644
--- a/frontend/main.c
+++ b/frontend/main.c
@@ -2977,7 +2977,12 @@ drm_process_layoutputs(struct wet_compositor *wet)
 	if (wet->require_outputs == REQUIRE_OUTPUTS_ALL_FOUND &&
 	    failed_layoutputs > 0)
 		return -1;
+
+	/* No layoutput means no output can currently be enabled. Keep
+	 * the compositor alive so a later hotplug can create the first output.
+	 * An attempted output which failed to enable must remain fatal. */
 	if (wet->require_outputs == REQUIRE_OUTPUTS_ANY &&
+	    failed_layoutputs > 0 &&
 	    failed_layoutputs == wl_list_length(&wet->layoutput_list))
 		return -1;
 
